  "code": "1036",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"149\" data-end=\"350\">The <strong data-start=\"153\" data-end=\"177\">Benzodiazepines test</strong> detects the presence of <strong data-start=\"202\" data-end=\"226\">benzodiazepine drugs</strong> in the body, typically via <strong data-start=\"254\" data-end=\"263\">urine</strong>, though it can also be done on <strong data-start=\"295\" data-end=\"321\">blood, saliva, or hair</strong> depending on clinical needs.</p>\n<p data-start=\"352\" data-end=\"378\">It is primarily used to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"379\" data-end=\"713\">\n<li data-start=\"379\" data-end=\"473\">\n<p data-start=\"381\" data-end=\"473\">Monitor <strong data-start=\"389\" data-end=\"421\">benzodiazepine use or misuse</strong> in clinical, rehabilitation, or forensic settings</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"474\" data-end=\"531\">\n<p data-start=\"476\" data-end=\"531\">Detect <strong data-start=\"483\" data-end=\"495\">overdose</strong> or <strong data-start=\"499\" data-end=\"511\">toxicity</strong> in emergency care</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"532\" data-end=\"646\">\n<p data-start=\"534\" data-end=\"646\">Ensure <strong data-start=\"541\" data-end=\"555\">compliance</strong> in patients prescribed benzodiazepines for anxiety, insomnia, seizures, or muscle spasms</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"647\" data-end=\"713\">\n<p data-start=\"649\" data-end=\"713\">Screen for <strong data-start=\"660\" data-end=\"679\">substance abuse</strong> or part of a <strong data-start=\"693\" data-end=\"713\">toxicology panel</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"715\" data-end=\"795\">Common benzodiazepines include diazepam, lorazepam, alprazolam, clonazepam, etc.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Possible Cause</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Clinical Significance / Context</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Therapeutic use</strong> (prescribed)</td>\n<td>Expected in patients taking benzodiazepines as directed for medical conditions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Acute or chronic misuse / abuse</strong></td>\n<td>Indicates non-prescribed or excessive use &rarr; risk of dependence, withdrawal, overdose</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Overdose</strong></td>\n<td>May lead to CNS depression, drowsiness, slurred speech, respiratory issues</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Cross-reactivity with other drugs</strong></td>\n<td>Some tests (especially immunoassays) may cross-react with non-benzodiazepine drugs</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"715\" data-end=\"795\"><strong>Note: </strong>Some benzodiazepines (e.g., clonazepam) may not be detected on standard urine drug screens due to different metabolic pathways. Confirmatory testing via GC-MS or LC-MS may be needed.</p>",
